  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation that coverage is accepted. If the claim was denied, talk to an Oregon attorney before considering appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask in writing for the full itemized estimate, not just the summary page."><span>Do you have the insurer’s complete, line-item estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get a line-item estimate from a contractor or estimator. A lump-sum bid is hard to defend in front of a panel."><span>Do you have your own itemized estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Gather every photo and note when each was taken. Add current photos too."><span>Do you have dated photos taken soon after the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Appraisal’ paragraph in the conditions and note any time limits."><span>Have you found and read the appraisal clause in your policy?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Suit Against Us’ condition and put the date on your calendar."><span>Do you know your policy’s deadline to file suit?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make reasonable temporary repairs (tarps, drying) and keep every receipt."><span>Are temporary repairs done and receipts saved?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request your declarations page from your agent or insurer."><span>Do you have your current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure attics, crawlspaces and wet walls have been checked so the scope is complete."><span>Has hidden damage been opened and documented?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Collect letters, emails and claim notes in date order."><span>Is your correspondence with the insurer organized by date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run your numbers in the appraisal payoff estimator. A small gap may not justify the cost."><span>Is the gap more than about 10% or $5,000?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Return any requested proof of loss on time."><span>If the insurer asked for a sworn proof of loss, has it been sent?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Reset answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="gauge-wrap">
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#e3e8f4" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#002a86" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3" style="transition:stroke-dashoffset .5s,stroke .3s"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint" style="text-align:center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Your to-do list</p>
        <ul data-o="todo" class="todo"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div>
<p class="hint">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout" style="padding-top:40px"><article class="prose">
<h2>How the score is weighted</h2>
<p>Coverage, estimates and evidence carry the most weight because they decide whether appraisal is the right tool and how well your number will hold up. Paperwork items matter but are easier to fix.</p>
<h2>What your result means</h2>
<ul><li><strong>75 and up:</strong> a strong file. A professional review of the gap is the next step.</li>
<li><strong>45 to 74:</strong> close the open items first; each one strengthens your position.</li>
<li><strong>Below 45:</strong> demanding appraisal now risks locking in a low number. Build the file first.</li></ul>

<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Are my answers saved?</summary><div class="a"><p>No. The checkup runs entirely in your browser and nothing is stored or sent.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I share the result with an appraiser?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. Take a screenshot or copy your to-do list and bring it to the first call.</p></div></details></div>
